-- title:
--   Unramified layer of the descended formal quotient tower
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ is a prime number, and the following blocks of data and hypotheses are in force.
--
--   **Base ring.** $\mathcal{O}$ is a commutative domain of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$ is irreducible (`hπ`), $\mathcal{O}$ is $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), the residue ring $\mathcal{O}/\pi$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal{O}$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a field of characteristic zero which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra and a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   **Unramified coefficients.** $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a commutative domain of characteristic zero and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, subject to: $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete (`hOnr_complete`), the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). Furthermore `vdet` is a homomorphism from $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ to $\mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) which, by `hvdet`, sends $g$ to $n$ exactly when $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal{O}$; thus `vdet` is the $\pi$-adic valuation of the determinant. Write $\mathcal{O}_2$ for the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ cut out as `AlgHom.equalizer` of $Fr \circ Fr$ and the identity, i.e. the elements fixed by $Fr^2$.
--
--   **Discrete cocompact group data.** $G$ is a group, $\sigma : G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ are homomorphisms with $\rho g$ the class of $\sigma g$ (`hρ`), and $\Gamma \le G$ is a subgroup containing a scalar element $z$ with `vdet`$(\sigma z) = 2$ (`hcent`) and an element $w$ with `vdet`$(\sigma w) = 1$ (`hodd`); $\Gamma'$ is the subgroup whose members are exactly the elements of $\Gamma$ with even `vdet` (`hΓ'`). The image $\rho(\Gamma')$ acts with finite vertex stabilisers on the vertices of the lattice tree of $\mathcal{O}$ in $K_0$ (`hdisc`) and with finitely many orbits (`hcocpt`). The matrix $g_1$ is the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$ (`hg₁`). The subgroup $N \le \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ satisfies $N \le \rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNle`), is normal as a subgroup of $\rho(\Gamma)$ (`hNnorm`) and has non-zero relative index in $\rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNidx`). Finally `DM` is a `MumfordTower 𝒪 π K₀ r g₁ N`: a tower of schemes $Z_n$ proper and flat over $\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1}$ with pullback transition squares, the affine-neighbourhood property, a functorial point map `DM.q` assigning to each $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with $(\pi)^{n+1} = 0$ and each Deligne datum over $B$ a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} B \to Z_n$, natural, compatible with the transitions, invariant under pullback by elements of $N$, together with its edge charts.
--
--   **The two-sheeted tower and the finite group.** $X : \mathbb{N} \to$ Scheme is a tower with structure morphisms $xb_n : X_n \to \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$ and transitions $xt_n : X_n \to X_{n+1}$, $G_2$ is a finite group acting by $a_n : G_2 \to \operatorname{Aut}(X_n)$, and there are morphisms $pr_1{}_n : X_n \to Z_n$ and $pr_2{}_n : X_n \to \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1})$, a homomorphism $\theta : \Gamma \to G_2$, and $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphisms $Fr_2{}_n$ of $\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1}$. The hypotheses on these are: the transition squares of $X$ over $\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+2} \to \mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1}$ are pullbacks (`hcart`); each $xb_n$ is proper (`hproper`) and flat (`hflat`); every finite set of points of $X_n$ lies in an affine open (`haff`); the $G_2$-action is over the base (`ha_over`) and commutes with the transitions (`ha_xt`); each square $(pr_1{}_n, pr_2{}_n, \mathtt{DM.zb}_n, \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1} \to \mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1}))$ is a pullback, so that $X_n$ is $Z_n$ base changed to $\mathcal{O}_2$ (`hX`); $xb_n$ is $pr_1{}_n$ followed by $\mathtt{DM.zb}_n$ (`hxb`); $pr_1$ and $pr_2$ are compatible with the transitions of $X$, of $Z$ and of $\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{\bullet}$ (`hxt₁`, `hxt₂`); $\theta$ is surjective (`hθsurj`) and $\theta\gamma = 1$ precisely when $\rho(\gamma) \in N$ (`hθker`); $Fr_2{}_n$ is induced by $Fr$ on $\mathcal{O}_2$ (`hFr₂`); the action of $\theta\gamma$ on the second factor is by $Fr_2{}_n$ raised to the power $-\,$`vdet`$(\sigma\gamma)$ (`ha_pr₂`); and on the first factor (`ha_pr₁`) for every $\gamma \in \Gamma$, every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with $(\pi)^{n+1} = 0$, all Deligne data $P, P'$ over $B$ with $P'$ the pullback of $P$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$ in the sense of `DeligneDatum.IsPullback`, and every $x : \operatorname{Spec} B \to X_n$ with $x$ followed by $pr_1{}_n$ equal to $\mathtt{DM.q}_n(P)$, the morphism $x$ followed by $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ and then $pr_1{}_n$ equals $\mathtt{DM.q}_n(P')$.
--
--   **The quotient tower and its point map.** `DQ` is a `TowerQuotientDatum 𝒪 π X xb xt G₂ a`: a tower $Y_n$ proper and flat over $\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1}$ with pullback transitions, together with finite surjective $G_2$-invariant morphisms $p_n : X_n \to Y_n$ exhibiting $Y_n$ as the quotient of $X_n$ by $G_2$, with the local universal property. The family $q$ assigns, for each $n$ and each $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ with $(\pi)^{n+1} = 0$, to each pair consisting of an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$ (an object of `AlgFunctor.prod (AlgFunctor.corep Onr) (Omega K₀ π)` at $B$) a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} B \to Y_n$. Its laws are: `hqdef`, which determines $q_n(\psi, P)$ as $x$ followed by $\mathtt{DQ.p}_n$ whenever $\psi_2 : \mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1} \to B$ induces $\psi$ on $\mathcal{O}_2$ and $x : \operatorname{Spec} B \to X_n$ satisfies $x \,;\, pr_1{}_n = \mathtt{DM.q}_n(P)$ and $x \,;\, pr_2{}_n = \operatorname{Spec}(\psi_2)$; `hqover`, that $q_n(x)$ followed by $\mathtt{DQ.yb}_n$ and then $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{O} \to \mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$ is the structural morphism $\operatorname{Spec} B \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}$; `hqnat`, naturality in $B$; `hqyt`, compatibility with the transitions $\mathtt{DQ.yt}_n$; and `hqinv`, invariance under the twisted action: for $\gamma \in \Gamma$ and $x, x'$ with `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct π Onr Fr vdet B (σ γ) x x'`, that is $x'_1 = x_1 \circ Fr^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma\gamma)}$ and $x'_2$ the pullback of $x_2$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$, one has $q_n(x') = q_n(x)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Write $A_n := \mathrm{chartERing}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}, \pi, r)/(\pi^{n+1})$, where $\mathrm{chartERing}(O^{\mathrm{nr}},\pi,r)$ is the localisation away from `edgeQuot.discr` of the quotient of the polynomial ring $O^{\mathrm{nr}}[X_0, X_1]$ by the edge relation, and $\pi$ denotes its image in that ring; $\xi$ and $\eta$ are the distinguished elements `chartERing.ξ` and `chartERing.η`. Then there exist a tower of schemes $Y^{\mathrm{nr}}_n$, morphisms $p_1{}_n : Y^{\mathrm{nr}}_n \to Y_n$ and $p_2{}_n : Y^{\mathrm{nr}}_n \to \operatorname{Spec}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi^{n+1})$, transitions $j_n : Y^{\mathrm{nr}}_n \to Y^{\mathrm{nr}}_{n+1}$, and, for every $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and every $n$, an open $U_{h,n} \subseteq Y^{\mathrm{nr}}_n$, a ring homomorphism $c_{h,n} : \Gamma(U_{h,n}, \mathcal{O}_{Y^{\mathrm{nr}}_n}) \to A_n$ and a morphism $\kappa_{h,n} : \operatorname{Spec} A_n \to Y^{\mathrm{nr}}_n$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   (1) For every $n$ the square formed by $p_1{}_n$, $p_2{}_n$, the composite of $\mathtt{DQ.yb}_n$ with $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{O} \to \mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$, and $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{O} \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi^{n+1})$ is a pullback; that is, $Y^{\mathrm{nr}}_n = Y_n \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}} \operatorname{Spec}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi^{n+1})$.
--
--   (2) $j_n$ followed by $p_1{}_{n+1}$ equals $p_1{}_n$ followed by $\mathtt{DQ.yt}_n$.
--
--   (3) $j_n$ followed by $p_2{}_{n+1}$ equals $p_2{}_n$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the reduction $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi^{n+2} \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi^{n+1}$.
--
--   (4) For all $h$ and $n$ the preimage $\kappa_{h,n}^{-1}(U_{h,n})$ is the whole of $\operatorname{Spec} A_n$, and, for any witness of the resulting inequality and any section $s$ over $U_{h,n}$, the element $c_{h,n}(s)$ is the image of $s$ under the comparison map of $\kappa_{h,n}$ on $U_{h,n}$, restricted to the total space and transported along the isomorphism between the global sections of $\operatorname{Spec} A_n$ and $A_n$. Thus $c_{h,n}$ is pullback of sections along the chart $\kappa_{h,n}$.
--
--   (5) For all $h$, $n$ and $y \in O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, applying $c_{h,n}$ to the restriction to $U_{h,n}$ of the pullback along $p_2{}_n$ of the global section of $\operatorname{Spec}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi^{n+1})$ corresponding to the class of $y$ gives the class of the image of $y$ in $A_n$; so the charts are compatible with the $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-structure supplied by $p_2$.
--
--   (6) For all $h$ and $n$ one has $U_{h,n} = j_n^{-1}(U_{h,n+1})$, and for any witness of the corresponding inequality and any section $s$ over $U_{h,n+1}$, the value $c_{h,n}$ of the restriction of $j_n^{\#}(s)$ equals the reduction of $c_{h,n+1}(s)$ under $A_{n+1} \to A_n$.
--
--   (7) (Chart points.) For all $h$ and $n$, every commutative ring $B$ that is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra and an $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra in a scalar tower, with $(\pi)^{n+1} = 0$ in $B$, every $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra homomorphism $\bar x : A_n \to B$ and all Deligne data $d, P$ over $B$: if $d$ lies in the standard edge chart with coordinates $\bar x(\xi), \bar x(\eta)$, namely $d.\mathrm{line}$ at the standard full lattice is the $B$-span of $\bar x(\xi) \otimes e_0 + 1 \otimes e_1$, $d.\mathrm{line}$ at $g_1 \cdot (\text{standard lattice})$ is the image under the base-changed action of $g_1$ of the $B$-span of $1 \otimes e_0 + \bar x(\eta) \otimes e_1$, and $d$ satisfies `DeligneDatum.InEdgeChart` for the pair $(g_1\cdot\text{std}, \text{std})$ (edge non-degeneracy at every prime of $B$), and if $P$ is the pullback of $d$ along $h^{-1}$, then $\operatorname{Spec}(\bar x)$ followed by $\kappa_{h,n}$ and then $p_1{}_n$ equals $q_n(B)$ evaluated at the pair consisting of the structure homomorphism $O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and $P$.
--
--   (8) For every $n$ the supremum of the opens $U_{h,n}$ over all $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is the whole of $Y^{\mathrm{nr}}_n$.
--
--   (9) For every $h$ the following two assertions hold. First, if $s$ and $s'$ are families of sections $s_m, s'_m$ over $U_{h,m}$, each compatible with the transitions in the sense that the restriction of $j_m^{\#}(s_{m+1})$ to $U_{h,m}$ is $s_m$ (and likewise for $s'$), and if $c_{h,m}(s_m) = c_{h,m}(s'_m)$ for all $m$, then $s = s'$. Second, for every family $\mathrm{fam}_m \in A_m$ compatible under the reductions $A_{m+1} \to A_m$, the existence of a transition-compatible family of sections $s_m$ over $U_{h,m}$ with $c_{h,m}(s_m) = \mathrm{fam}_m$ for all $m$ is equivalent to the following invariance condition: for every $m$, every commutative ring $B$ which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra and an $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra in a scalar tower with the image of $\pi$ nilpotent, all $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra homomorphisms $\bar x, \bar x' : A_m \to B$ and all Deligne data $d, d', P, P'$ over $B$ such that $d$ lies in the standard edge chart with coordinates $\bar x(\xi), \bar x(\eta)$ and $d'$ lies in it with coordinates $\bar x'(\xi), \bar x'(\eta)$ (both in the sense of (7), including the edge non-degeneracy condition), $P$ is the pullback of $d$ along $h^{-1}$, $P'$ is the pullback of $d'$ along $h^{-1}$, and there exists $\gamma \in \Gamma'$ with $P'$ the pullback of $P$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$, one has $\bar x(\mathrm{fam}_m) = \bar x'(\mathrm{fam}_m)$.
--
--   This is the unramified layer of the Čerednik–Drinfeld construction of the formal quotient: it base changes the finite-group quotient tower $Y$ of the Mumford tower to the complete unramified ring $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, equips the result with Mumford's edge charts indexed by $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ compatibly with the point map $q$, and identifies the inverse limit of the sections over a chart open with those compatible families of functions on the edge chart ring that take equal values at $\Gamma'$-related chart points. It is used in the assembly of the formal quotient datum together with the adic coefficient data, namely by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_formalQuotientDatum_coeff_adicFib_of_mumfordTower_of_towerQuotientDatum`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_formalQuotientDatum_coeff_adicFib_of_mumfordTower_of_towerQuotientDatum).
